MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Traced defects fixed:
- Source: CSV (local clock, UTC+2) compared against TimeCurrent() (broker, UTC+3) — every
  blackout window sat 1h early. Replaced with CalendarValueHistory/CalendarEventById, which
  return broker server time. Inp_Global_VETO_NewsFile, ParseNewsDateTime, MonthToInt removed.
- Default was UseNews=false + MED_PLUS: the filter shipped OFF, and if switched on would have
  blocked medium-impact events too. Now true + NEWS_IMPACT_HIGH_ONLY, 60/60.
- Dead decoys removed from SEA_TradeExecutor.mqh: m_news_events[]/m_news_count (never populated,
  never read), NewsImpactPass() (hardcoded MED+, zero callers), GetSymbolCurrencies() (naive 3+3
  name slice, zero callers, would have failed on a broker naming gold GOLD).
- Impact is now the typed ENUM_CALENDAR_EVENT_IMPORTANCE, not a parsed string.
- Refresh is per-bar, rate-limited, and discarded whole if any currency leg fails (a partial
  refresh would silently drop one currency's events while looking healthy).
- Fail-open + loud alert on calendar failure; loud banner when inert in the Strategy Tester.

READMEs updated: README.md, README_SEA_VETO_REFERENCE.md (§1a), README_SEA_PARAMETER_MAPPING.md
